This bug is caused by faulty hoisting logic. [Here's a simpler repro](https://svelte-5-preview.vercel.app/#H4sIAAAAAAAAE52QzQqDMBCEXyWEHiwUvPsHfY7ag8YNhOquJKvQhrx7o1KF0lNvO7PfsMN6qU0PTmY3L7EZQGbyOo7yIvk5LsLN0DNE7WiyanEKp6wZuaqxZkXoWDgmC6IUPuTRjLaeULEhFJooOQu_eDWvWL7Np0OEr0zb2D8yrwRmQN6D6-UPW6RHZyzaiTlmCDPVG_UofWRDpXpyUKTbsvqFxWIRI9TGDjsYPzNQZ7SBTmZsJwj38AYpESA5VAEAAA==):

```svelte
<script>
	const store = {};

	function foo() {
		store;
		$store;
	}

	function bar() {
		store;
		$store;
	}

	function baz(event) {
		foo();
	}
</script>

<button on:click={foo}>close</button>
<button on:click={bar}>confirm</button>
```

Output:

```js
function bar(_, store, store, $store) {
	store;
	$store();
}
```

(An aside: interestingly, `foo` isn't hoisted, even though it's only referenced by `baz`, which _could_ be hoisted but isn't, presumably because the hoisting logic never encounters it.)
